{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons","id":977152,"title":"Dragon Bloods are Daemons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T06:52:49-07:00","id":977152,"title":"Dragon Bloods are Daemons?","content":"Something that just clicked for me right now which I think is mildly fascinating. Thought I'd share.<br /> <br /> Ok so Yozi's are defeated &quot;Primordials&quot;.<br /> - 3rd Circle Daemons are the highest form of their souls made physical<br /> - 2nd Circle Daemons are further dilutions of the 3rd<br /> - 1st Circles are essentially offshoots of the 2nd<br /> <br /> <br /> Now consider that Gaia IS a Primordial and remains to be one to this day. And that during the primoridal war she helped the Gods by:<br /> - Creating 5 Elemental Dragons (i.e.: her &quot;3rd Circle&quot; Daemons)<br /> - Her Elemental Dragons empowered 40 Males and 160 Females each who were massive breeders (i.e.: her &quot;2nd Circle Daemons&quot;)<br /> - These 1,000 Dragon-Blooded Progenitors bred the first Terrestrial Army for the Primordial War (i.e.: 1st Circle daemons being &quot;offspring&quot; of the 2nd Circles)<br /> <br /> <br /> Naturally the name &quot;Daemon&quot; doesn't exactly apply to the Dragon-Blooded, but its an interesting parallel. Could be worth a story-thread to some Storytellers. Or it could be ignored by everyone who reads this :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:04:07-07:00","id":977159,"title":"","content":"When you get down to it, there's not much difference between a god and a first circle demon. Both are spiritual entities made by primordials for a specific purpose.<br /> <br /> So really, by this metric, everyone is demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:13:13-07:00","id":977163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977159#post977159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get down to it, there's not much difference between a god and a first circle demon. Both are spiritual entities made by primordials for a specific purpose.<br /> <br /> So really, by this metric, everyone is demons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lol. This did make me legit lol. I like it. EVERYONE IS A DAEMON!<br /> <br /> Could be a good basis for a theology to be spread by Infernal Exalts methinks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T08:02:27-07:00","id":977178,"title":"","content":"An interesting thought, but they're not really a parallel in the sense that the 5 Elemental Dragons are not part of Gaia's soul hierarchy, but her &quot;children&quot;. What that means is anyone's guess, but they exist outside of the concept of &quot;circles&quot; in the way demons do.<br /> <br /> As for this being a theology spread by infernals, I'm skeptical 95% of scholars know what a Primordial is, and even fewer know who Gaia is or that she made the elemental Dragons who begot the Dragon Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12025-praxiscat","name":"PraxisCat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12025_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T08:07:49-07:00","id":977182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977159#post977159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get down to it, there's not much difference between a god and a first circle demon. Both are spiritual entities made by primordials for a specific purpose.<br /> <br /> So really, by this metric, everyone is demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>But especially John Stalvern. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3LKadZ4LFU\" target=\"_blank\">Like, woah</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:31:06-07:00","id":977215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PraxisCat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977178#post977178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting thought, but they're not really a parallel in the sense that the 5 Elemental Dragons are not part of Gaia's soul hierarchy, but her &quot;children&quot;. What that means is anyone's guess, but they exist outside of the concept of &quot;circles&quot; in the way demons do.<br /> <br /> As for this being a theology spread by infernals, I'm skeptical 95% of scholars know what a Primordial is, and even fewer know who Gaia is or that she made the elemental Dragons who begot the Dragon Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that, due to the Immaculate Philosophy, a lot of scholars would know that Gaia is an ancient and lovely being who was the mother of the 5 Elemental Dragons.<br /> And she is either the Goddes-esque being of Creation itself, or is actually Creation (like, everyone lives on Gaia). Not that these necessarily are right (it's entirely possible the Dragons are her soul hierarchy, it's just not known, but equally they could be her children in the sense that they're things she created... or perhaps they're literally her children, like she birthed them with one of her world-bodies), but that's what people will think.<br /> But of course, she gets a lot less attention than the Dragons.<br /> Maybe like Gaia in Greek myth: she was the Goddess of the Earth, and all the titans and gods were his descendants, but despite being one of the original two beings, she wasn't a big figure in Hellenic religion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:41:33-07:00","id":977224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977215#post977215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually think that, due to the Immaculate Philosophy, a lot of scholars would know that Gaia is an ancient and lovely being who was the mother of the 5 Elemental Dragons.<br /> And she is either the Goddes-esque being of Creation itself, or is actually Creation (like, everyone lives on Gaia). Not that these necessarily are right (it's entirely possible the Dragons are her soul hierarchy, it's just not known, but equally they could be her children in the sense that they're things she created... or perhaps they're literally her children, like she birthed them with one of her world-bodies), but that's what people will think.<br /> But of course, she gets a lot less attention than the Dragons.<br /> Maybe like Gaia in Greek myth: she was the Goddess of the Earth, and all the titans and gods were his descendants, but despite being one of the original two beings, she wasn't a big figure in Hellenic religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Alternative is that the Siderials covered up Gaia and kept the Dragons... Because they didn't want a cult forming that Indirectly worshiped Gaia. Esspecially if Gaia has disappeared.. who knows what could happen if the &quot;Matron mother of the Dragons&quot; returned and had the Dragonblooded Cult bend to her wishes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:14:29-07:00","id":977239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977224#post977224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Alternative is that the Siderials covered up Gaia and kept the Dragons... Because they didn't want a cult forming that Indirectly worshiped Gaia. Esspecially if Gaia has disappeared.. who knows what could happen if the &quot;Matron mother of the Dragons&quot; returned and had the Dragonblooded Cult bend to her wishes...</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine if she returned the Terrestrials going over to her is the not the biggest of the available problems. While the dragonblooded <i>might,</i> Luna <i>will</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:20:18-07:00","id":977241,"title":"","content":"Gaia never showed any interest in human society before, I don't think the Sidereals have any indication to think that would change.<br /> <br /> I don't see that the Sidereals would be particularly bothered by a Gaia-worshipping cult, but since Gaia doesn't answer human prayers, it's never going to be big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T10:24:44-07:00","id":977242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977239#post977239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine if she returned the Terrestrials going over to her is the not the biggest of the available problems. While the dragonblooded <i>might,</i> Luna <i>will</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was trying to say.. that's the reason that she's not mentioned in the Immaculate text.... If the Dragons are perfect beings, then the Mother of Dragons must be more perfect then they. To save the hassle of dealing with that.. they just omit that bit from the history books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:16:42-07:00","id":977265,"title":"","content":"I could see an old immaculate text or two mentioning that the, &quot;Elemental Dragons Were Born of GAIA, From Whom The World Was Birthed.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that being a point of philosophical debate among some monks. <br /> <br /> Some might cast Gaia as some mysterious boring, the living embodiment of the world.<br /> <br /> Others might say that Gaia is an abstract concept- an raw, vital and elemental state from which the elemental dragons emerged. <br /> <br /> Still others might say that Gaia is just a name for the gestalt form of all the elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:18:32-07:00","id":977266,"title":"","content":"Let's be fair the biggest concern that the Sids would have had with Gaia somehow ending up as the revered figure of the DBs would be that Gaia would be likely to acquiesce to certain parties making requests. The whole lunar anathema thing would be rather tricky to maintain if Gaia gave Luna authority to control the Immaculate Faith while she was out. Before anyone says whether or not that would happen, I'm just saying that such a thing would likely have been a concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:02:48-07:00","id":977285,"title":"","content":"If she's had a jouten in Yu-Shan all this time and knows exactly what's happening, then she's as apathetic as the Incarnae and there's little chance of her ever intervening. On the other hand, if she's entirely gone and comes back one day, who knows!<br /> <br /> Gaia probably doesn't care about the details of human society, but seeing her beautiful Creation reduced to a smashed ruin riddled with shadowlands and Wyld zones like cancer, she might be moved to do... something.<br /> <br /> Maybe give Luna and the Lunars explicit authority over the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Maybe wake up her Dragons and tell them to drastically reorganize divine, elemental, and DB societies to protect Creation better.<br /> <br /> Maybe just say &quot;Oh Nirguna no&quot; and do something cosmic that fixes all the shadowlands and Wyld zones and dragon lines, but also incidentally causes gigantic <s>natural</s> elemental disasters everywhere. &quot;Oops, that caused a mass exctinction. Well that's life! I'll just replace whatever died with kaiju, superweeds, and super insects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;<br /> <br /> I doubt she'd let humanity go extinct because that would deprive Luna of her Chosen... but if Gaia is moved to act, it would probably suck for everyone currently in power. And most of everyone else, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-27-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:02:33-07:00","id":977446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977242#post977242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was trying to say.. that's the reason that she's not mentioned in the Immaculate text.... If the Dragons are perfect beings, then the Mother of Dragons must be more perfect then they.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that follows. Is Mary &quot;more perfect&quot; than Jesus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:13:44-07:00","id":977504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977446#post977446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how that follows. Is Mary &quot;more perfect&quot; than Jesus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was Mary a Titan among later gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:19:15-07:00","id":977508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977285#post977285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe just say &quot;Oh Nirguna no&quot; and do something cosmic that fixes all the shadowlands and Wyld zones and dragon lines, but also incidentally causes gigantic <s>natural</s> elemental disasters everywhere. &quot;Oops, that caused a mass exctinction. Well that's life! I'll just replace whatever died with kaiju, superweeds, and super insects. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is almost explicitly the effect of releasing the Kukla. In between the tale the size of kingdoms wiping the earth clean and head the size of mountains unleashing literal rivers of fire. Everywhere Kukla's scales fall heals shadowlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:40:35-07:00","id":977517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977504#post977504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Mary a Titan among later gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Were Titans not gods?<br /> <br /> (Rhetorical question; the Titans <i>were</i> in fact gods.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T18:53:18-07:00","id":977521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons#post977152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that just clicked for me right now which I think is mildly fascinating. Thought I'd share.<br /> Ok so Yozi's are defeated &quot;Primordials&quot;.<br /> - 3rd Circle Daemons are the highest form of their souls made physical<br /> - 2nd Circle Daemons are further dilutions of the 3rd<br /> - 1st Circles are essentially offshoots of the 2nd<br /> <br /> Now consider that Gaia IS a Primordial and remains to be one to this day. And that during the primoridal war she helped the Gods by:<br /> - Creating 5 Elemental Dragons (i.e.: her &quot;3rd Circle&quot; Daemons)<br /> - Her Elemental Dragons empowered 40 Males and 160 Females each who were massive breeders (i.e.: her &quot;2nd Circle Daemons&quot;)<br /> - These 1,000 Dragon-Blooded Progenitors bred the first Terrestrial Army for the Primordial War (i.e.: 1st Circle daemons being &quot;offspring&quot; of the 2nd Circles)<br /> <br /> <br /> Naturally the name &quot;Daemon&quot; doesn't exactly apply to the Dragon-Blooded, but its an interesting parallel. Could be worth a story-thread to some Storytellers. Or it could be ignored by everyone who reads this :P<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The way First Circle Demons are created are almost entirely different from the way Dragonblooded are conceived, born and Exalted. I don't think first circle demons can pro-create amongst themselves either. Dragonblooded are human and Exalted.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:57:29-07:00","id":977549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977521#post977521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think first circle demons can pro-create amongst themselves either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends - does impaling yourself on a spike, consuming lethal amounts of poison, donating &quot;material&quot; to a neomah, et cetera., count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T21:13:50-07:00","id":977588,"title":"","content":"Many First Circle species can procreate themselves, and any of them can reproduce using Neomah. They mostly don't reproduce the way animals or plants do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T22:32:28-07:00","id":977604,"title":"","content":"The Five Elemental Dragons are not Third Circle Souls. They have no connection to Gaia's soul hierarchy. They are the Five Elemental Dragons. The Dragonblooded are Exalted Humans, not First Circle Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:23:38-07:00","id":977724,"title":"","content":"As noted already, the Dragons aren't souls, so it's moot on this. Note also that the origin of Dragon-Blooded in the 2e hardcover is kind of conterversial to an extent. And doesn't fit with the general nature of how Second Circle Demons work anyhow. 200 breading bots is not what 2CDs tend to be. Hell, most unquesitonable have only seven and thsoe seven are specific facets of the the higher demon's personality, not smething created for a task.<br /> <br /> And the Dragon-Blooded themselves are human and Exalted, first, and foremost. Any theories fo them actually being demons or some fancy god-blood tends to, in my mind, arise from their being unique amongst the Exalted in that they Exalt through procreation. That there are even discussions like this due to the &quot;One of these is not like the other...&quot; thing of Dragon-Blooded is actually part of why we got a buncha new Exalts this edition.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:35:18-07:00","id":977727,"title":"","content":"First of all, I believe the term would be Daeva, rather than Demon. The latter is kind of a yozi-specific variant.<br /> <br /> But to call them deva implies they are somehow part of the soul hierarchy of the primordial... Which they clearly aren't. Just as the gods aren't.<br /> <br /> Daeva is not &quot;created by this primordial dude&quot;. Daeva is one of the souls of the gestalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T06:46:56-07:00","id":977733,"title":"","content":"Also, Exalted generally doesn't spell &quot;demon&quot; with an &quot;a.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:02:02-07:00","id":977738,"title":"","content":"Also there's no difference between first generation dragon blooded and the third or fourth or fifth. That's kind of the whole point of them. The power doesn't dilute like it would in a god blooded. So it doesn't make sense to call gen 1 the second circle and everyone else the first.<br /> <br /> At most, taking a few non-canon theories as true, the dragonblooded are empowered by the essence of heavily-modified former-daeva, which makes them closer to Autochthonian subroutines than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:25:25-07:00","id":977748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977517#post977517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were Titans not gods?<br /> <br /> (Rhetorical question; the Titans <i>were</i> in fact gods.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure what it is you're arguing for, since the point stands that Mary was human, while Gaia, not so much. In fact, it seems that you might have shot the thesis of your prior post in the foot arguing that titans were gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:46:22-07:00","id":977760,"title":"","content":"I think the issue here is that there are two schools of thought. That the parent of a child must be greater than the child (perhaps the titans, and any hero-king ever because who can measure up to a hero?), and that the child must grow up to be greater than their parents (the Buddha, Jesus, the hopes of many a parent I know). And neither is really wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, no offense, but I <i>will</i> ignore the whole &quot;Dragon-Blooded are demons&quot; thing. I don't think it's a really useful direction of discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:23:21-07:00","id":977777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977760#post977760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, no offense, but I <i>will</i> ignore the whole &quot;Dragon-Blooded are demons&quot; thing. I don't think it's a really useful direction of discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more an interesting thought project as to a possibility that I doubt will ever be explored in Canon. I know in first edition the Dragon Bloods would have eventually became the Kuei-Jin or &quot;Ten thousand Demons&quot; but that seems to be more an effect of the Dynasty Charms that the Scarlet empress would have had and not... being related to Gaia.<br /> <br /> Side note.. they Might be exploring a portion of what happens to the Dragonblooded if their higher souls are torn away and replaced if Gloam is any indication... (Only really a couple of paragraphs on the City/Harbour/Locale but I hope they go into it abit more, then again the Mystery is better if they don't go into it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":3981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","user":"RickmanUK","date":".  Remembered the name of the charm type. 09-28-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:24:34-07:00","id":977779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977748#post977748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not quite sure what it is you're arguing for, since the point stands that Mary was human, while Gaia, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mary was the mother of Jesus, and was not &quot;more perfect&quot; (already a contradiction in terms) than Jesus. Her divinity or lack thereof is irrelevant. Someone can be the parent of someone else without being that someone's spiritual better, and there's no reason to assume the Immaculate Philosophy teaches any different in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977748#post977748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it seems that you might have shot the thesis of your prior post in the foot arguing that titans were gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Like I said, divinity is kind of irrelevant - indeed, the Immaculate Philosophy teaches that the gods are just kinda there, and are not in and of themselves <i>deserving</i> of worship just by being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:33:52-07:00","id":977783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977779#post977779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mary was the mother of Jesus, and was not &quot;more perfect&quot; (already a contradiction in terms) than Jesus. Her divinity or lack thereof is irrelevant. Someone can be the parent of someone else without being that someone's spiritual better, and there's no reason to assume the Immaculate Philosophy teaches any different in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>True and it does depend on the way they teach it, I Suspect they don't actually touch on Gaia at all, if they do it's probably as some eponymous/vague &quot;Mother of Dragons&quot; entity that simply vanished after she created them. It allows for more focus upon the Dragons and what they represent and not upon living up to a being that does little and doesn't interact with mortals, Live up to those that you can and not up to those that you cannot, For such is the order of Things.<br /> <br /> Flowery for flowery sake... No they aren't Demons, but that doesn't mean they couldn't have been in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:06:29-07:00","id":977797,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Gaia had the Dragons, which are her children, create the Dragonblooded instead of her souls so she can claim plausibility deniability to the other Primordials. <br /> <br /> &quot;So... about these humans that keep poking me. They seem to be empowered by your elemental power.&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>My</i> elemental power? Talk to my children, not me. I don't have anything to do with this.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:16:05-07:00","id":977824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977797#post977797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Gaia had the Dragons, which are her children, create the Dragonblooded instead of her souls so she can claim plausibility deniability to the other Primordials.<br /> <br /> &quot;So... about these humans that keep poking me. They seem to be empowered by your elemental power.&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>My</i> elemental power? Talk to my children, not me. I don't have anything to do with this.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it as something more like...<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey... Gaia... you know these.. Pests?&quot;<br /> &quot;What pests?&quot;<br /> &quot;These mortals full of Elemental power.... Your Power&quot;<br /> &quot;My Power? You are saying I would empower these.. Rebels?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well yes.&quot;<br /> &quot;How Dare you... Screw you and all of your Stuff.. I'm going to my Room! Never have I been....&quot; *Trails off as she wonders off into her garden*<br /> &quot;But! But...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:11:26-07:00","id":977927,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> But the DBs act human in a lot of ways and create human off-spring rather than god-blooded...<br /> <br /> What if the DBs themselves are not the first circle demons? What if their Exaltations are the first circle demons and the DB as a whole is actually a conjoined being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:19:36-07:00","id":977933,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded are humans. And are indistinguishable from mortals until they Exalt. Their Exaltation is of their blood and them, not something external. I think that the idea that the Terrestrial Exaltation is some demon grafted on the bloodline is again, not really in line with Exaltations in general, nor is it really much use save to in a sense make Dragon-Blooded &quot;not real Exalted&quot;.<br /> <br /> As a note, this is part of why I kind of hate that origin story in the 2e DB book and the emphasis in 2e that there's some racial purity thing where DBs aren't really humans, just some other species that's 100% genetically compatable with humans. It makes them more some weird elf elemental hybrdi thing isntead of a lineage people who have real histories and such.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:25:14-07:00","id":977935,"title":"","content":"How would it being a demon grafted on their bloodline make them not exalted? As far as I can tell a human soul with some variation of spirit mumbo jumbo grafted onto it is pretty much exactly what an exalted is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:00:15-07:00","id":977956,"title":"","content":"It's a very <i>specific</i> variation of spirit mumbo-jumbo. You can't just glue a ghost to someone and call it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:08:26-07:00","id":977963,"title":"","content":"Celestial Exaltations are the person receving an Exaltation, which was held by some previous hero, which empowers them and gives themt heir Second Breath. Nothing has ever been said that the spiritual mumbo jumbo being grafted to you is how Exaltation occurs. This is also the language used for things like the Deathlords in relation to the Neverborn and Akuma.<br /> <br /> However, since early 1e, the fact that DBs <i>don't</i> have some external mechanism save lineage, folks have over the years had tried to find one. Thsi begs the question that Exaltation = something stuck to your soul.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals break this as well, note, since they have perfectly normal souls just in extraordinary bodies. And 3e is introducing other kinds of Exalted with non-Celestial origins like Liminals to further hammer home the idea that Exaltation is <i>not</i> grafting random spiritual mumbo jumbo to people.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:39:09-07:00","id":978036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977963#post977963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mumbo jumbo</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977956#post977956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mumbo-jumbo</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Not Quite Simple Soul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977935#post977935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mumbo jumbo</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zWRykybDpYA\" data-code=\"zWRykybDpYA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zWRykybDpYA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:23:32-07:00","id":978754,"title":"","content":"I think the proper analogy for the Dragon-Blooded would be a hypothetical Chosen of one of Adorjan's daughters. Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:13:43-07:00","id":978812,"title":"","content":"This gives me an idea for a Rakan-Thulio-style big-bad who makes Exigent-lite lieutenants by trapping demons/gods/elementals in Yasal crystals, then grafting them onto humans in such a way that they go through a process kind of like the Chrysalis Grotesque and come out with spirit powers and weird mutations.<br /> <br /> I don't know why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:31:30-07:00","id":978866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=977963#post977963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, since early 1e, the fact that DBs <i>don't</i> have some external mechanism save lineage, folks have over the years had tried to find one. Thsi begs the question that Exaltation = something stuck to your soul.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals break this as well, note, since they have perfectly normal souls just in extraordinary bodies. And 3e is introducing other kinds of Exalted with non-Celestial origins like Liminals to further hammer home the idea that Exaltation is <i>not</i> grafting random spiritual mumbo jumbo to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I liked about 2e was that it discussed that despite DBs theoretically being entirely based on lineage, for some reason it seemed like more heroic and extraordinary DBs took their Second Breath than ones who sat around getting fat and being lazy. It wasn't explicit about it, but being heroic improving your chances is a good thing for DBs as a whole, or you get the whole fan mentality where no DB deserves power because clearly they're all just well bread lazy inheritors.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals don't really have 'normal' souls, they have souls that have been in the same gem for thousands of years, and lived through hundreds of heroic lives, and then they're implanted into a super magical body via a process that connects to Autochthon himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:05:12-07:00","id":978878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=978866#post978866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things I liked about 2e was that it discussed that despite DBs theoretically being entirely based on lineage, for some reason it seemed like more heroic and extraordinary DBs took their Second Breath than ones who sat around getting fat and being lazy. It wasn't explicit about it, but being heroic improving your chances is a good thing for DBs as a whole, or you get the whole fan mentality where no DB deserves power because clearly they're all just well bread lazy inheritors.<br /> <br /> Alchemicals don't really have 'normal' souls, they have souls that have been in the same gem for thousands of years, and lived through hundreds of heroic lives, and then they're implanted into a super magical body via a process that connects to Autochthon himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think of it as dragon's blood being an ember of latent divinity within every potential DB's being. Some of them are hot enough to eventually ignite on their own; others need a little stoking first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:46:54-07:00","id":978964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=978754#post978754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the proper analogy for the Dragon-Blooded would be a hypothetical Chosen of one of Adorjan's daughters. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the name of the internet, explain yourself man!! :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:31:16-07:00","id":978978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=978866#post978866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the things I liked about 2e was that it discussed that despite DBs theoretically being entirely based on lineage, for some reason it seemed like more heroic and extraordinary DBs took their Second Breath than ones who sat around getting fat and being lazy. It wasn't explicit about it, but being heroic improving your chances is a good thing for DBs as a whole, or you get the whole fan mentality where no DB deserves power because clearly they're all just well bread lazy inheritors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue with this myself is it runs against some of the example Exaltations we had gotten before. Mainly that Dragon-Blooded society is super-lethal for lazy kids anyways, and so there was already more a cultural feature rather than some metaphysical feature to Terrestrials getting the Second Breath. It also kind of assumes htis concept of meritocracy to the Exaltation that I don't thinkw as part of it. It also seems to draw from a bit of the idea of &quot;The IO is a little right&quot; that I noticed crept in as time went on. <br /> <br /> I kind of actually prefer the 1e ambiguity of things. Especially since to me, talent and scuh only get you so far at a young age. This idea that the Exaltation for Dragon-Blooded predicts greatness of character also feels off when you have characters like Cathak Chenow around. I just don't see what is gotten by saying that they <i>deserve</i> Exaltation on some level, when to me the whole point of it being a bloodline thing is to call into question the legitimacy of power by inheritance to some extant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/977152-dragon-bloods-are-daemons?p=978866#post978866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals don't really have 'normal' souls, they have souls that have been in the same gem for thousands of years, and lived through hundreds of heroic lives, and then they're implanted into a super magical body via a process that connects to Autochthon himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing about an Alchemical soul that isn't substantially different than anyone else's soul. It's a matter, again, of achievement rather than some inherent quailtiy of greatness to that person determined in its creation. Which is why in the context of my original quote the whole idea that Exaltation is stapling something fancy to someone's soul is not really a good descriptor save Celestial Exalted, who no longer are the &quot;default&quot; kind of Exalted save in the sense that Solars are first published.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:37:22-07:00","id":978981,"title":"","content":"I prefer Dragonblooded Exaltation Events to be less heroic and more stress triggered. Your teacher pisses you off, you may exalt. Young Dynasts do stupid shit in their late teens to trigger Exaltation (and often die in the process). I always head canon'ed that the Seventh Legion has an insanely stressful boot camp to weed out potential Dragonblooded. If you don't exalt after 8 weeks of hell, you ain't going to Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:29:40-07:00","id":979105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-ic